.TH qsh-config-set 1  "set 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-config\-set \- Write one key. The edited file must pass the same validation the daemons apply at startup, or nothing is written. Comments and key order in `config.toml` are kept
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh config set\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write one key. The edited file must pass the same validation the daemons apply at startup, or nothing is written. Comments and key order in `config.toml` are kept
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Dotted key path, e.g. `serve.bind`
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
The new value. A string key keeps it verbatim, an integer key takes decimal digits, a boolean key takes `true` or `false`
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
